{title: 418 - Day of Judgment, Day of Wonders!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #418 • UNSER HERRSCHER • 9.7.8.7.4.7}
{lyricist: John Newton}
{composer: Joachim Neander}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 418}
{meta: tune UNSER HERRSCHER}
{meta: meter 9.7.8.7.4.7}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm/D]Day [Dm]of judgement, day [Bb]of [Eb]wonders!
[Bb]Hark [Adim]the [Bb]trumpet's awful sound,
[Bb/F]Louder than [Dm/A]a [Bb]thousand [Eb]thunders,
[Bb]Shakes the vast creation [Adim]round!
[Bb]How [Cm]the [Gm]summons
[Gm]Will [Eb]the sinner's [Gm]heart [Cm/G]confound!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm/D]See [Dm]the Lord [Bb/F]in [Eb/Bb]the [Dm/A]glory [Eb]nearing,
[Bb]Clothed [Adim]in [Bb]majesty divine,
[Bb/F]You [Eb/Bb]who [Bb]long [Dm/A]for [Bb]His [Eb]appearing,
[Bb]Then [Adim]shall [Bb]say, "This God is [Adim]mine!"
[Bb]Gracious [Cm]Savior, [Gm]Gracious [Gbm]Savior,
[Gm]Own [Eb]me in [F]that [Gm]day [Cm/G]as [F]Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm/D]At [Dm]His [Bb/F]call the dead awaken,
[Bb]Rise [Adim]to [Bb]life form earth and sea!
[Bb/F]All [Eb/Bb]the [Bb]powers of [Eb]nature [Dm/A]shaken
[Bb]By [Adim]His [Bb]looks prepare to [Adim]flee.
[Bb]Careless [Cm]sinner, [Gm]Careless [Gbm]sinner,
[Gm]What [Eb]will then [F]become [Cm/G]of [F]thee?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm/D]But [Dm]to [Bb/F]those [Eb/Bb]who [Dm/A]have [Eb]confessed
[Bb]Loved [Adim]and [Bb]served the Lord below,
[Bb/F]He [Eb/Bb]will [Bb]say, [Dm/A]"Come [Eb]near, ye [Dm/A]blessed,
[Bb]See [Adim]the [Bb]kingdom I bestow;
[Bb]You forever, [Gm]You forever
[Gm]Shall [Eb]my love [F]and [Gm]glory [F]know."
{end_of_verse}
